+# Risk Terminal regression tests
+
+After installing this backend workspace's existing development dependencies, run from its root:
+
+```sh
+node --test apps/engine/src/battle/risk-terminal-regression.cjs
+```
+
+The existing engine test recipe also includes these eight cases through `risk-terminal-regression.spec.ts`:
+
+```sh
+pnpm --filter engine exec node --test -r ts-node/register src/battle/risk-terminal-regression.spec.ts
+```
+
+The harness resolves TypeScript and ts-node from the engine workspace and reads this checkout's actual publisher and shared projection source. It does not need a compiled shared package, model, API server, PostgreSQL, Redis connection or credentials. It uses in-memory database/Redis doubles and TypeScript transpile-only loading. It is not a full backend typecheck or settlement integration test.
+
+Coverage: buffered real versus RPC/NPC classification, persisted fallback, missing/invalid price, buffer read failure, malformed buffer entries, and publication identity/time. Changes to the source are exercised directly; there are no machine-specific paths or external fixture folders.
